
==========================================================================
  CONTROL FROM DISTRIBUTIVITY — E2E DEMO
==========================================================================

  ctrl(f) = undist ∘ (id ⊕ (id_I ⊗ f)) ∘ dist
  Pipeline: OCaml Linear DSL → Bridge → Python → pytket

==========================================================================
  CIRCUIT: Abstract ctrl(f)
==========================================================================

  ctrl(f) : Bool ⊗ A → Bool ⊗ A

              ┌───────┐ ┌───────────────┐ ┌─────────┐
  q[0] Bool ──┤       ├─┤               ├─┤         ├──
              │ dist  │ │ id ⊕ (id ⊗ f) │ │ undist  │
  q[1] A   ──┤       ├─┤               ├─┤         ├──
              └───────┘ └───────────────┘ └─────────┘

  dist, undist : 0 gates (wire permutations)
  omap0 dispatches by tag qubit:
    |0⟩ branch → id   (do nothing)
    |1⟩ branch → f    (apply f to payload)

==========================================================================
  CIRCUIT: Unoptimised ctrl(f)  [identity branch not elided]
==========================================================================

  PlusMap compiles id ⊕ (id ⊗ f) as:
    • anti-control for |0⟩:  X on tag, controlled-id body, X on tag
    • control for |1⟩:       controlled-f body

  When left body = id (0 gates), anti-control emits a bare X–X pair:

           ┌ anti-ctrl (|0⟩) ┐ ┌ ctrl (|1⟩) ┐
           │                  │ │             │
  q[0] ────X────────────X─────●───────────────
           │                  │ │             │
  q[1] ──────────────────────⊕───────────────
           │                  │ │             │
           └──────────────────┘ └─────────────┘

  The X–X pair is a no-op: it cancels to identity.
  Total naive gates: 3  (X, X, CX)

  The compiler elides the X–X when the branch body has 0 gates,
  yielding the optimised circuit:

  q[0] ──●──
          │
  q[1] ──⊕──

  Optimised: 1 gate  (CX)

==========================================================================
  LEVEL 1: ctrl(X) — CX  (2 qubits)
==========================================================================
  Naive (anti-control on identity branch not elided):
2 qubits, 4 gates
  X q[0]
  CRz q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CX q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]
  Optimised (identity branch elided):
2 qubits, 1 gates
  CX q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]

  Verification: ctrl(X) = CX ?
    eq_circ: EQUAL (fidelity=1.000000)

==========================================================================
  LEVEL 2: ctrl(ctrl(X)) — CCX  (3 qubits)
==========================================================================

  Abstract:
    dist_l(I,I,Bool⊗Q) ; omap0(id, id_I ⊗ ctrl(X)) ; undist_l

    omap0 left  (|0⟩): id                       → 0 body gates
    omap0 right (|1⟩): id_I ⊗ ctrl(X)           → ctrl(X) body gates

  Naive:
3 qubits, 9 gates
  X q[0]
  CX q[0, 1]
  CRz q[0, 2]
  CX q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CX q[0, 1]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2]
  CX q[0, 1]
  CCX q[0, 1, 2]
  perm: [0, 1, 2]
  Optimised:
3 qubits, 1 gates
  CCX q[0, 1, 2]
  perm: [0, 1, 2]

  Verification: ctrl²(X) = CCX ?
    eq_circ: EQUAL (fidelity=1.000000)

==========================================================================
